{"id":"diagram-revision-06bb3a2c-616c-4104-ac3e-876dd7e5dd45","diagramId":"diagram-5d2bc009-df74-4f64-a3d4-75d756b9582f","parentId":"diagram-revision-a849b15f-57a6-426b-92dc-62e17d22034e","diagram":{"id":"overview","revision":2,"diagramId":"diagram-5d2bc009-df74-4f64-a3d4-75d756b9582f","revisionId":"diagram-revision-06bb3a2c-616c-4104-ac3e-876dd7e5dd45","content":{"revisionId":"overview:2","ascii":"Saved CanvasViews and branching\n|\n+-- A named view remembers saved work; the canvas history owns its state\n|   `-- CanvasHistory.record owns the durable records\n|       +-- canvasViews: names, active view, ancestry and working-copy pointers\n|       |   `-- Each saved view points into shared checkpoint storage\n|       |       +-- startCheckpointId / checkpointIds: origin and saved steps\n|       |       `-- finalCheckpointId: latest explicitly saved state\n|       +-- snapshots: canvas composition and exact diagram bindings\n|       |   `-- diagramBindings -> diagramRevisions: content needed to rebuild it\n|       `-- workingCopies[viewId] -> checkpoint with edits left on that view\n|           `-- Stored separately from its saved endpoint; switching retains both\n|\n+-- User actions activate changes through one command path\n|   `-- CanvasViewControls -> onCommand -> CanvasViewReceiver.apply\n|       +-- Calls controller.canvasView with the current document version\n|       |   `-- CanvasHistory.canvasView dispatches the requested operation\n|       |       +-- Create: name the current canvas and make that view active\n|       |       |   `-- Stash outgoing work; pin current state as the first save\n|       |       +-- Save: make the active canvas the view's saved endpoint\n|       |       |   +-- Retain earlier checkpoints; append this one if new\n|       |       |   `-- Clear the view's working-copy pointer\n|       |       `-- Open: resume the chosen view through openCanvasView\n|       |           +-- Calls stashCanvasView for the outgoing active view\n|       |           |   `-- Preserve its current edits as a working copy\n|       |           `-- Resolve target state, then activate a fresh checkpoint\n|       |               +-- NEEDS target working copy, if one exists\n|       |               |   `-- Otherwise NEEDS the target's saved endpoint\n|       |               `-- Carry the current camera across the switch\n|       `-- Receiver retains a request receipt, then calls persist\n|           `-- Retrying the same request saves without applying the action twice\n|\n+-- Branching grows a family from a precise saved state\n|   +-- Fork NEEDS the parent's latest saved checkpoint\n|   |   +-- Unsaved parent work stays with the parent; save first to include it\n|   |   `-- Create one child, then call openCanvasView to begin editing it\n|   `-- Alternatives NEED the same pinned checkpoint for every sibling\n|       +-- Create independent children as one group; leave current canvas open\n|       |   `-- This copies saved state; generation is a separate operation\n|       `-- Example family: Base at saved checkpoint S\n|           +-- Option A: child of Base, forked at S\n|           |   `-- A refinement: child of A, forked at A's later saved state\n|           `-- Option B: child of Base, also forked at S\n|               `-- Editing B does not change A, Base, or checkpoint S\n|                   \n|   Ancestry is stored on each child\n|   +-- parentViewId -> which view it came from\n|   +-- forkCheckpointId -> the exact state it inherited\n|   `-- alternativeGroupId -> which candidates belong to the same choice\n|\n`-- Choosing a branch uses those relationships to determine what survives\n    +-- Keep Option A: a user choice within an alternative group\n    |   +-- Resume A if needed; save its current state and clear its working copy\n    |   `-- NEEDS group membership to find B, then ancestry to find B's descendants\n    |       +-- Archive those other branches recursively\n    |       `-- Keep A and A's refinement available; Base remains available\n    +-- Discard A: archive A and every descendant, including its refinement\n    |   `-- If the active view lies in that archived branch\n    |       +-- Open the discarded view's available parent\n    |       `-- If no parent is available, stash work and clear the active view\n    `-- Archiving hides views from the explorer while retaining saved history\n        `-- Existing saved checkpoints remain immutable\n\nTree depth expresses ownership, nested calls and branch ancestry.\nNEEDS marks data dependencies across those structures: restoring requires\ncheckpoint content; pruning requires group membership and parent links.","asciiSha256":"d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332","structure":{"kind":"tree","parserVersion":"ascii-tree-2","rootIds":["overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-1"],"nodes":{"overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-1":{"id":"overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-1","label":"Saved CanvasViews and branching","line":1,"branchColumn":-1,"startColumn":1,"endColumn":31,"childIds":["overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-3","overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-14","overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-33","overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-51"],"foldRanges":[{"startLine":2,"endLine":66}]},"overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-3":{"id":"overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-3","label":"A named view remembers saved work; the canvas history owns its state","line":3,"branchColumn":0,"startColumn":5,"endColumn":72,"parentId":"overview:2:d9adee12cdd8f0515e12ea0c988a59736bef1daa6833d9c0bd91b66a3e1db332:line-1","childIds":